[2026-11-18] rc:4617893493 inline on src/wallet/wallet.cpp by polespinasa (member) (edited 2026-11-18):
in 15fa33740799875801707e6c8e06ff5ed480dbf1 wallet: add -walletpar option

Maybe we should just throw here if `m_wallet_par` is negative? I think we should require `-walletpar` to be bigger than `-GetNumCores()` and smaller than `GetNumCores() + 1`.

Also `GetIntArg` returns an int64 while `m_wallet_par` is a normal int you can overflow the integers and trick a bit the result. This obviously is weird and not critic, but I think is worth addressing as is easy to fix:

```diff
$ git diff
diff --git a/src/wallet/wallet.cpp b/src/wallet/wallet.cpp
index b1b9f52919..56e106afb5 100644
--- a/src/wallet/wallet.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/wallet.cpp
@@ -2930,14 +2930,14 @@ bool CWallet::LoadWalletArgs(std::shared_ptr<CWallet> wallet, const WalletContex
     wallet->m_notify_tx_changed_script = args.GetArg("-walletnotify", "");
     wallet->SetBroadcastTransactions(args.GetBoolArg("-walletbroadcast", DEFAULT_WALLETBROADCAST));

-    wallet->m_wallet_par = args.GetIntArg("-walletpar", DEFAULT_WALLETPAR);
-    if (wallet->m_wallet_par <= 0) {
+    int64_t wallet_par = args.GetIntArg("-walletpar", DEFAULT_WALLETPAR);
+    if (wallet_par <= 0) {
         // '0' means 'autodetect'
         // '<0' means leave that many cores free
-        wallet->m_wallet_par += GetNumCores();
+        wallet_par += GetNumCores();
     }
     // The calling thread counts towards -walletpar, as for -par.
-    wallet->m_wallet_par = std::clamp(wallet->m_wallet_par, 1, MAX_WALLETPAR + 1);
+    wallet->m_wallet_par = static_cast<int>(std::clamp<int64_t>(wallet_par, 1, MAX_WALLETPAR + 1));

     return true;
 }

